	"notes": "Framer's own homepage (which, fittingly, is built with Framer) is a dark, one-column marketing page: a headline and a live-looking AI chat demo up top, then a row of trusted-by logos, then several repeating sections that pair some text with a picture. The whole thing never gets wider than 1200 pixels no matter the monitor — an ultrawide screen just gets more black space on the sides, the same trick several other marketing and blog sites in this set use. The one unusual thing here is how late the mobile menu appears: most sites switch to a hamburger icon around 768px, but this page waits until 410px, so it keeps its full text menu on nearly every phone.",
